cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived software release,
  the associated research article, and the associated dataset.
title: >-
  MATLAB software for non-destructive audible spectral analysis of
  aqueous fructose solutions
type: software
abstract: >-
  MATLAB R2020a research software associated with the 2021 Applied
  Sciences article "Study of the Optimal Waveforms for Non-Destructive
  Spectral Analysis of Aqueous Solutions by Means of Audible Sound and
  Optimization Algorithms". The spectrum-data-processing component
  prepares the input information required by the classifier. The
  classifier is executed through programa.m and applies a grouping
  genetic algorithm with an Extreme Learning Machine fitness function
  to extract acoustic frequencies for classifying fructose
  concentrations in distilled water. The optional third-party
  visualization function bubbleplot.m is not distributed.
